From 76f46c3a5d88bf77fc002982edabf955175052d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:35:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wayland: Use the size the compositor configures

vkmark took the output's mode for fullscreen and set the output's
wl_output.scale as buffer scale. With a fractional output scale, which
wl_output.scale rounds up, the image then covers only part of the
screen: on a 1080x2400 phone at scale 2.27 (configure 476x1058,
wl_output.scale 3) it showed at 360x800 in the top left corner.
In a window, a buffer scale that does not divide the requested size
(800x600 at scale 3) is a protocol error, and the compositor
disconnected vkmark.

Wait for the first configure before choosing the swapchain extent.
Fullscreen takes the output's pixels and shows them at the configured
size through wp_viewporter; a configured window size is used with the
output's scale; otherwise the buffer scale is only set when it divides
the size, else the viewport (or no scaling) shows the buffer.
---
 src/meson.build                  |  16 ++++
 src/ws/wayland_native_system.cpp | 151 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/ws/wayland_native_system.h   |  14 +++
 3 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index a2da205..a8cef22 100644
